> DMS Settings - Personalization

In-depth guide to the personalization section of DMS settings (super+S > personalization).

### Wallpaper

set wallpaper per-monitor or per-mode (light/dark).
the wallpaper script (*super+W*) sets wallpapers by group folder.
per-mode or per-monitor settings will override the script's behavior.

### Color Sources

Auto (matugen): automatically generates a color scheme from your wallpaper.
Manual: you pick the primary/accent colors directly.
Custom: specify custom hex colors.
Registry: uses colors from a registry file.

### Matugen Palette Options

material you color palette variants:
vibrant - balanced vibrant colors (default)
muted - soft, desaturated colors
tonal - single-hue tonal palette
neutral - grayscale/neutral palette
vibrant_dark - vibrant but darker tones
expressive - more saturated, expressive colors

each produces a different look from the same wallpaper. experiment with these.

### Dark/Light Mode

toggle with *super+shift+T* or in settings.
matugen generates separate palettes for light and dark mode.
per-mode wallpapers let you set different wallpapers for light/dark.

### GTK/QT Theme Application

GTK themes are applied via adw-gtk-theme (libadwaita).
QT themes via qt6ct-kde and kvantum.
if theming is not working, click the fix button at the bottom of the themes page.
for vesktop: enable theme in vencord settings, toggle theme to refresh.
for VSCode/code-oss: may need manual theme selection.

### Font Settings

set system font, monospace font, and interface font sizes.
fonts with nerd font icons are recommended (CaskaydiaCove NFM, FiraCode Nerd).

### Animations

enable/disable DMS UI animations (independent of mango window animations).
animation speed and style settings for DMS panels and transitions.
